This wasn't really about "Oh, I'm wimpy and I need a crutch", it was
"oh, that's annoying, wait, wouldn't a deity want you to put up altars 
for 'em as a sign of your faith?" and the idle thought of "wouldn't 
it be neat to spell things out with _s?".

[snip]

My view is the "too easy" aspect[1] is just a matter of twiddling balance
and making the creation suitably expensive.   A number of interesting
/ways/ of creating altars have been proposed, some harder, some easier,
and it's been vastly entertaining, but most of 'em have been /hard/,
which seems contrary to what a supposed deity would want.

And it would be neat to take stuff that isn't of much use in the game,
and give it some use.  Want to make it harder to ascend by building
altars?  Require the use of candles: you might use too many, and 
screw your chances of ascending.  (While hallucinating, read a blessed 
scroll of earth while standing on five candles for a chaotic altar, six 
for neutral, or seven for lawful).

<shrug>

It was a Neat Idea, not a Proposed Fix For Being Too Hard.

[1] Which seems to be undermined by the "many atheist ascensions"
argument -- if it's hardly an issue to not use 'em and still ascend,
then what's the problem with having 'em?

